  "entries": [
    {
      "id": "ost-d0",
      "type": "definition",
      "text": "Heat is familiar to all of us. We can feel heat entering our bodies from the summer Sun or from hot coffee or tea after a winter stroll. We can also feel heat leaving our bodies as we feel the chill of night or the cooling effect of sweat after exercise.",
      "source": "openstax",
      "sourceUrl": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/1-1-temperature-and-thermal-equilibrium",
      "sourceTitle": "OpenStax UP2: Termodinámica",
      "tier": "TIER_1_ACADEMIC",
      "authorityScore": 95,
      "relevanceScore": 90
    },
    {
      "id": "ost-d1",
      "type": "definition",
      "text": "What is heat? How do we define it and how is it related to temperature? What are the effects of heat and how does it flow from place to place? We will find that, in spite of the richness of the phenomena, a small set of underlying physical principles unites these subjects and ties them to other fields. We start by examining temperature and how to define and measure it.",
      "source": "openstax",
      "sourceUrl": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/1-1-temperature-and-thermal-equilibrium",
      "sourceTitle": "OpenStax UP2: Termodinámica",
      "tier": "TIER_1_ACADEMIC",
      "authorityScore": 95,
      "relevanceScore": 90
    },
    {
      "id": "ost-d2",
      "type": "definition",
      "text": "A thermometer measures its own temperature. It is through the concepts of thermal equilibrium and the zeroth law of thermodynamics that we can say that a thermometer measures the temperature of something else, and to make sense of the statement that two objects are at the same temperature.",
      "source": "openstax",
      "sourceUrl": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/1-1-temperature-and-thermal-equilibrium",
      "sourceTitle": "OpenStax UP2: Termodinámica",
      "tier": "TIER_1_ACADEMIC",
      "authorityScore": 95,
      "relevanceScore": 90
    },
    {
      "id": "ost-d3",
      "type": "definition",
      "text": "Explain thermal equilibrium",
      "source": "openstax",
      "sourceUrl": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/1-1-temperature-and-thermal-equilibrium",
      "sourceTitle": "OpenStax UP2: Termodinámica",
      "tier": "TIER_1_ACADEMIC",
      "authorityScore": 95,
      "relevanceScore": 90
    },
    {
      "id": "ost-d4",
      "type": "definition",
      "text": "Explain the zeroth law of thermodynamics",
      "source": "openstax",
      "sourceUrl": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/1-1-temperature-and-thermal-equilibrium",
      "sourceTitle": "OpenStax UP2: Termodinámica",
      "tier": "TIER_1_ACADEMIC",
      "authorityScore": 95,
